<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Tarbelli</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aquitanian people of the Adour basin and the Landes coast, known for river gold and the hot springs of Dax.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Tarbelli were one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquitani">Aquitani</a>, the peoples between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> who spoke a language related to Basque. They held the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adour">Adour</a> valley and the Atlantic shore around modern Dax and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayonne">Bayonne</a>. Known chiefly from Caesar, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> describes rich gold deposits in their land, with nuggets found in shallow pits and river sands. Their hot springs at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquae-tarbellicae">Aquae Tarbellicae</a> (Dax) became famous under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. No central capital is recorded before the Roman period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Tarbelli submitted to Caesar's legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 56 BCE after his campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a>. Under Augustus they formed a civitas with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquae-tarbellicae">Aquae Tarbellicae</a> as its chief town, which later became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Dax.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tarbelli.jpg" alt="Tarbelli" width="320" height="274"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aquitani_tribes_map-fr.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aquitanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd></dl></aside></div>

